Sorry for the typos:
in (4):  "if you have NO evidence ..."
In (5): "Test whether (4) fits significantly better than (3)."

I add: 
(6) If you have specific hypotheses about correlation parameters, you may be able to test just those correlation parameters and keep the rest at zero.

Finally, note that correlation parameters are linked to  the design (or model) matrix. They depend on what you pick as the intercept; they are NOT invariant to transformations of covariates, linear or non-linear. 

Reinhold Kliegl

